## Features

* **Every launcher at once.** Finds MultiMC, PolyMC and Prism Launcher on its own and lists the instances from all of them.
* **Recent first.** Instances are sorted by when you last played them, with your total play time alongside.
* **Fuzzy matching.** `mc atm` finds All the Mods 9.
* **Your icons.** Built-in, custom and modpack icons show up next to each instance.
* **Portable installs.** Point it at any launcher folder or `.exe` and it reads the instances from there.
* **Context menu.** `Shift+Enter` on an instance to open its folder or the launcher itself.

## Usage

Type `mc` to see your instances, most recently played first:

```
mc
```

{{ screenshot("screenshot", alt="Minecraft instances listed in Flow Launcher") }}

Keep typing to search, then press `Enter` to launch:

```
mc create
```

{{ screenshot("search", alt="Searching Minecraft instances in Flow Launcher") }}

## Installation

### Flow Launcher

In Flow Launcher, type:

```
pm install minecraft multi launcher
```

{{ screenshot("install", alt="Flow Launcher plugin manager installing Minecraft Multi Launcher") }}

### Manual installation

Download the zip from the [latest release]({{ project.url }}/releases/latest) and unzip it into
`%appdata%\FlowLauncher\Plugins`, then restart Flow Launcher.

## Settings

The plugin looks for launchers in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs`, `%LOCALAPPDATA%`, `%APPDATA%`,
`Program Files` and Scoop. If yours lives somewhere else, set **Launcher folder** in the plugin
settings to the folder that contains `MultiMC.exe`, `polymc.exe` or `prismlauncher.exe` (or to
the `.exe` itself). Only that launcher is used while the setting is filled in.

## Development

```
tox                    # tests on every supported Python
tox -e screenshots     # re-render .github/assets with flow-render
tox -e readme          # re-render README.md
python scripts/build.py --zip build/MC-Multi-Launcher.zip
```

Release notes live in [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md).
